{
  "schema": "triergon.codecs.correctness-manifest.v1",
  "reference": "ffmpeg-play-views-native",
  "contract": [
    "Probe and demux the full container and decode the chosen video and audio tracks through the facade example and the pinned FFmpeg 9.0.2 reference.",
    "Matroska and MP4 use the playback engine packet view. MPEG-TS uses the facade source access-unit reader, because the transport playback engine does not supply that view.",
    "Compare every RGBA canvas byte and each picture presentation timestamp in output order. Require identical stereo s16 sample counts and rates and apply the existing audio_device_path LSB bound.",
    "Compare every packet in demux order by stream ordinal, time base, signed PTS, DTS, duration, key flag, byte length and payload MD5. Matroska packet ticks are expressed in nanoseconds. Compare differences in source and reference-derived clocks as open cases.",
    "Use a 1920 by 1080 canvas. The 640 by 360 example canvas is outside this grade until there is pixel parity across the corpus.",
    "Both workers use explicit stream ordinals for three-tracks.mkv. The fixture rights and inputs are inherited from the existing authored corpora.",
    "The two private ATSC audio stream types use the declared ATSC namespace. The DVB E-AC-3 input uses its service profile."
  ],
