  "open_case_readings": {
    "three-tracks": "Matroska CodecDelay and BlockDuration are source facts. The pipeline retains nanosecond clocks and discards 16 samples from the first selected AAC block. The native demuxer reports rounded clocks and its decode returns the complete first block.",
    "avc-high-b": "Matroska DefaultDuration is in nanoseconds. The decoded canvases and presentation order match while the source durations or missing DTS differ from the native demuxer packets in Segment ticks.",
    "hevc-b1": "Matroska DefaultDuration is in nanoseconds. The decoded canvases and presentation order match while the source durations or missing DTS differ from the native demuxer packets in Segment ticks.",
    "avc-seek": "Matroska DefaultDuration is in nanoseconds. The decoded canvases and presentation order match while the source durations or missing DTS differ from the native demuxer packets in Segment ticks.",
    "avc-aac-quicktime-surround": "ISO/IEC 14496-12 edit lists map media time to presentation time. The pipeline uses source media times. It also reaches an idle decode session before the full suffix where FFmpeg completes both streams.",
    "avc-aac-quicktime-reordered": "ISO/IEC 14496-12 edit lists map media time to presentation time. The pipeline uses source media times. It also reaches an idle decode session before the full suffix where FFmpeg completes both streams.",
    "encoded-hevc-aac-front": "The ISO BMFF sample rows match. The pipeline publishes no picture or PCM output on the supplied HEVC/AAC configuration. The reference decodes two pictures and two AAC frames, leaving the configuration-to-session seam open.",
    "baseline-stereo": "H.222.0 PES headers carry selected PTS/DTS anchors. The source AU reader keeps unanchored clocks absent. The reference derives per-packet times and durations. The delivered RGBA and stereo PCM outputs match their numeric rules.",
    "media-00": "H.222.0 PES headers carry selected PTS/DTS anchors. The source AU reader keeps unanchored clocks absent. The reference derives per-packet times and durations. The delivered RGBA and stereo PCM outputs match their numeric rules.",
    "replay-avc-ac3-00": "H.222.0 PES headers and A/52 coded frames distinguish source clock anchors from derived timing. The strict AU reader and FFmpeg can report different packet clocks or order. The stereo PCM grade retains every sample.",
    "replay-avc-eac3-00": "H.222.0 PES headers and A/52 coded frames distinguish source clock anchors from derived timing. The strict AU reader and FFmpeg can report different packet clocks or order. The stereo PCM grade retains every sample.",
    "dvb-hevc-eac3-32000": "H.222.0 PES headers and A/52 coded frames distinguish source clock anchors from derived timing. The strict AU reader and FFmpeg can report different packet clocks or order. The stereo PCM grade retains every sample."
  },
